# EDA Summary Report

## Data Cleaning

* Checked missing values
* Removed duplicate records
* Encoded categorical features
* Applied feature scaling using StandardScaler

## Statistical Analysis

* Mean
* Median
* Mode
* Variance
* Standard Deviation

## Analysis

* Customer purchase behavior analysis
* Correlation between features
* Comparison of customer attributes affecting purchase decisions

## Key Findings

* Customer purchasing behavior is influenced by multiple features.
* Some variables show a positive correlation with the purchase outcome.
* Data preprocessing improved the quality of the dataset.
* Feature scaling enhanced the performance of machine learning models.
* Logistic Regression, KNN, and Decision Tree models were trained and compared to identify the best-performing model.

## Conclusion

EDA helped understand customer purchasing patterns, identify important features, and prepare the dataset for machine learning. The cleaned and processed data improved prediction accuracy and enabled the development of an effective customer purchase prediction model.
